SPEC §3, §8, §9, §7 "Deploy details". Moo base class. Attributes: k8s (default Client::Sync), resolver, upstream (coderef or spec), crd, crd_class, namespace (from CR metadata / attribute, no scope mapping), config (spec.config), configurable label prefix (default comb.internal/ per §14 proposal) and managed-by value. Contract methods with defaults: name, depends_on, endpoints, manifests, check, bridge_manifests, stub_class; optional class method upstream. from_crd($crd, %opts) with k8s, resolver, upstream, stub; loads spec.class at runtime; stub => sub selects stub_class; stub_class default "${class}::Stub" only if that class loads. Contract check at construction: a stub missing any endpoint name of its original dies naming the missing ones. Lifecycle ops (all Futures, never throw): deploy (inject labels on objects and hashrefs; set namespace on namespaced resources that lack it), status (derived from pods: waiting/terminated reasons, restart counts, PodScheduled=False; Succeeded Job pods must not count as unhealthy; a Comb whose manifests contain no workloads is healthy once its resources exist; readiness = containers ready, not only pod phase Running), healthy, logs (tail lines, multi-pod headers, previous container on CrashLoop), restart (pod template annotation <prefix>restartedAt RFC3339 on Deployment/StatefulSet/DaemonSet; Jobs deleted), stop (Deployments/StatefulSets to 0, CronJobs suspended, Jobs deleted), describe, endpoint($name) (local: cluster = service.namespace.svc:port, service default = comb name, overridable per endpoint). Not in scope: reconcile (k4). Proto (~/dev/proto lib/HI/Comb.pm, lib/HI/Comb/Backend/K8s.pm; old IO::K8s, inspiration only) selected pods by app= label; use the comb label instead.

